🛠 Three‑Tier Architecture
This setup now includes:

Frontend (Nginx) — serves static assets and proxies API requests.

Backend (Python Flask) — provides API endpoints and connects to DB.

Database (Postgres) — persistent data storage.


🚀 Run Full Stack

docker-compose up --build -d

Frontend: http://localhost:8080

Backend API: http://localhost:8080/api/users

Database: accessible at localhost:5432 (user: postgres, password: postgres)

🔗 Networking
All services share app-network.

Backend connects to DB via service name db.

Frontend proxies API requests to backend (api:5000).

💾 Volumes
nginx-logs → persists frontend logs.

db-data → persists Postgres data.

📉 Optimization
Lightweight base images (nginx:alpine, python:3.11-slim, postgres:15-alpine).

Multi‑stage build keeps frontend image small.

Compose orchestrates networking and persistence automatically.

This gives you a complete three‑tier Docker Compose stack: frontend, backend, and database


